    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Disciplinary case",
          "heading": "Sam Prendergast cited over Fiji hip-drop tackle, risking Springboks test absence",
          "body": "Ireland fly-half Sam Prendergast was cited after the 43-15 win over Fiji for a hip-drop tackle on captain Peceli Yato in the first half, an incident that went unpunished on the day. The 23-year-old now faces a disciplinary process that could keep him out of the South Africa game in Dublin. Springboks head coach Rassie Erasmus says the tackle should have been a red card, yet he expects Prendergast to play: \"I think there is going to be a technicality and he is going to play.\""
        },
        {
