    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Man of the match",
          "heading": "James Botham named man of the match as Wales beat All Blacks",
          "body": "Wales blindside flanker James Botham was named man of the match in the 35-28 win over New Zealand, a first victory over the All Blacks in 73 years. Once play resumed he was everywhere, tackling, scrambling and springing back up. His Wales debut came against Georgia in November 2020 at an empty Parc y Scarlets, and injuries and competition later kept him out of the side for more than two and a half years. Former Wales and Lions captain Sam Warburton, who has watched him since he first came to Cardiff, rates his footwork for contact."
        },
        {
