          "kicker": "Discipline test",
          "heading": "Sclavi and Elías yellow cards: Pumas hold on to beat Italy",
          "body": "Joel Sclavi and Efraín Elías were both shown yellow cards three minutes apart in the final quarter, leaving the Pumas playing with thirteen for an extended spell. Elías's card also handed Italy a penalty try, and Argentina had to dig deep to hold on. Pablo Matera kept his players relatively calm while Italy pressed for a comeback. The 19-14 win was the second of the 2026 Nations Championship."
        },
