          "kicker": "Gainline problem",
          "heading": "Les Kiss' Wallabies lost the collisions that mattered at Murrayfield, Gallan argues",
          "body": "Gallan's Guardian analysis of the 15-12 loss points to the gainline as the core failure. One lineout sequence near Scotland's 22 around the 66th minute shows it: after nine phases Australia had gone roughly five metres backwards, and after 18 phases the move ended with a turnover by Rory Darge. Kiss had already flagged the problem after the England defeat, saying, \"We gave them too much at the gainline for sure.\""
