          "kicker": "Co-captain's story",
          "heading": "Warner Dearns, who left New Zealand aged 14, co-captained Japan at Twickenham",
          "body": "The second row's route to Saturday's Twickenham captaincy began with a reluctant move: his father Grant took a strength and conditioning job with NEC Green Rockets, and 14-year-old Dearns said he did not want to leave New Zealand. Having qualified on residency grounds, he debuted for Japan in November 2021 at 19 and featured in all four matches at the 2023 Rugby World Cup. This year he spent a season's sabbatical at the Hurricanes, helping Wellington to their first Super Rugby title in a decade."
        },
