          "kicker": "Selection debate",
          "heading": "Taine Randell: Barrett, Mo'unga could have played final Tests after Wales loss",
          "body": "Speaking on The Platform NZ podcast, former All Blacks captain Taine Randell said Beauden Barrett and Richie Mo'unga could have played their final Tests against Wales in Cardiff. Barrett started at full-back and captained New Zealand at Test level for the first time, while Mo'unga, in his 58th Test, wore the No. 10 jersey. Randell pointed to thin cover at first-five, with Ruben Love injured and four players who are all first-fives. He added that the younger players will get more chances."
        },
